Non-Transactional Leisure & Cultural Activities
When survival metrics (hunger, energy) are satisfied, agents engage in non-transactional leisure activities that do not require economic output:
Cultural Creation (CREATE_CULTURAL_WORK): Writing poetry, painting signs, woodcarving, composing lore. Restores cultural_fulfillment and reduces overwork_counter.
Quiet Exploration & Reflection: Visiting favorite places, walking along riverbanks, idling near warm hearths.
Communal Care & Gift-Giving: Offering food, remedies, or supportive conversation to sick or overworked neighbors.

